  "notes": [
    "Transcribed from the official PDF (semester table with credits and prerequisites on page 2). The two JPGs are an unofficial student-made 'Latest Course Map' (NSU Faculty Course & Grade Analysis) without semesters, per-course credits or prerequisites, so they were used only for cross-checking.",
    "The document prints no category names; categories were inferred from its colour coding (green = General Education, purple = Math & Science, red = Major Core, bold brown = Capstone, orange = Electives). CSE115, CEE110 and EEE452 are coloured with the Math & Science group.",
    "BEN205 (alternative to ENG115) and HIS103 (alternative to HIS101) come from the JPGs, which print 'BEN 205/ENG115' and 'HIS 103/HIS101'; their titles are not printed in any source and were filled in from NSU course names.",
    "The JPGs also differ from the PDF in ways not encoded here: they list EEE154 (in School Core, no CEE110), EEE498 Internship/Co-op (1 credit), BIO103 as 3 credits without lab, and group courses as GED 34 / School Core 38 / EEE Core 42 / Capstone 4 / Internship 1 / Specialized Electives 9 / Open Elective 3 (these group totals add to 131-134 rather than 130, so they look inconsistent).",
    "The JPGs list five specialized-elective trails for ELECT1-3 (Solid state electronics: EEE410/411/413/414/415/491; Power system: EEE461/462/464/465/468/492; Communication: EEE422/424/426/427/428/493; Robotics and Intelligence system: EEE453/432/433/436/468/494; Telecommunication: EEE331/421/423/451/471/495). They are not listed as rows.",
    "ENG103 prerequisite 'ENG102/Waiver' is stored as ENG102.",
    "EEE499A requires '100 credits completed'; the sequence page adds 'and all core courses', which is not encoded in the rule.",
    "EEE321 prerequisite printed as 'EEE221, MAT361' is read as both.",
    "'SOC101/ANT101/ENV203(GEO205)' is one slot; ENV203 and GEO205 appear to be the same course under two codes, both listed as alternatives.",
    "Lab suffixes (+CL, +IL) were dropped; credits are as printed (combined where the map prints them combined)."
  ],
